1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:11,630
A 67-year-old with new breathlessness. A child with fever and
petechiae. Every shift brings cases that are genuinely
uncertain.

2
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:19,836
The knowledge to help is already there — buried in thousands
of past encounters, and unreachable at the bedside.

3
00:00:20,036 --> 00:00:24,106
ClinIQ AI was built to close that gap.

4
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:30,274
Nowhere is that gap sharper than in an emergency department.

5
00:00:30,474 --> 00:00:37,424
One clinician, dozens of patients, and a specialist who will
not be free for hours.

6
00:00:37,624 --> 00:00:45,558
ClinIQ AI makes the time before specialist input clinically
productive instead of clinically passive.

7
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:52,948
When a case is submitted, ClinIQ AI does not simply forward it
to a language model.

8
00:00:53,148 --> 00:01:01,490
It embeds the case, then performs a similarity search over
your existing encounters, scoped to the specialty.

9
00:01:01,690 --> 00:01:11,472
Those real cases become grounding context. Guideline-based
reasoning, weighed against what this hospital has actually
seen.

10
00:01:11,672 --> 00:01:18,742
No vector store configured yet? It degrades gracefully and
still works from day one.

11
00:01:20,090 --> 00:01:29,104
Start with the patient. Type an MRN and ClinIQ AI pulls the
record straight from the EHR.

12
00:01:29,304 --> 00:01:38,630
Demographics, medications, problem list and prior history
arrive pre-filled — resolved only within your own
organisation.

13
00:01:38,830 --> 00:01:45,468
Choose one of eight specialties, or paste a referral letter as
free text. Then ask.

14
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:54,178
The response is never loose prose. It is a structured record,
and the schema is enforced.

15
00:01:54,378 --> 00:02:03,656
A summary. Red flags, or an explicit empty list.
Investigations grouped with the rationale for each one.

16
00:02:03,856 --> 00:02:13,230
A prioritised action plan — immediate, short-term, follow-up —
and safety netting that says exactly when to escalate.

17
00:02:13,430 --> 00:02:19,084
And a badge: informed by four similar cases from this
institution.

18
00:02:19,284 --> 00:02:24,602
That number tells the clinician how much of this assessment
came from here.

19
00:02:25,950 --> 00:02:33,212
Every differential carries a likelihood, the features
supporting it — and the features arguing against it.

20
00:02:33,412 --> 00:02:42,330
With references to real published guidance: NICE, the ESC, the
ACC and AHA.

21
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:46,288
It is built to be challenged, not just read.

22
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:55,646
ClinIQ AI does not admit patients. Admission raises a request,
and a doctor decides.

23
00:02:55,846 --> 00:03:03,420
The named doctor is notified, the case enters the pool, and
its status stays visible to the whole team.

24
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:10,088
A reviewing doctor accepts the case and talks to the clinician
who raised it.

25
00:03:10,288 --> 00:03:18,054
Here the registrar asks about prior imaging — and learns the
echo eighteen months ago was entirely normal.

26
00:03:18,254 --> 00:03:24,292
Re-analysis feeds the original case and the full conversation
back through the model.

27
00:03:24,492 --> 00:03:34,802
Aortic stenosis drops. Diastolic function rises. The earlier
analysis is kept in history — nothing is overwritten.

28
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:41,252
When the doctor commits to a diagnosis, the assessment narrows
onto it.

29
00:03:41,452 --> 00:03:48,426
No competing differentials — just confirming, staging and
managing the condition in front of them.

30
00:03:48,626 --> 00:03:54,352
And the finished record is written back to the EHR as a
clinical note.

31
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:59,698
Some patients need a facility this one is not.

32
00:03:59,898 --> 00:04:11,384
Transfer runs in four steps — receiving facility filtered by
capability, clinical details, transport level, and the EMTALA
checklist.

33
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:19,686
ClinIQ AI generates the SBAR handoff and the full
documentation pack automatically.

34
00:04:19,886 --> 00:04:24,340
The paperwork stops being the thing that holds the ambulance.

35
00:04:25,690 --> 00:04:31,248
For clinical leads, the dashboard shows what no single shift
can see.

36
00:04:31,448 --> 00:04:41,182
Admissions against discharges, average length of stay, bed
occupancy, and the conditions actually arriving at your door.

37
00:04:41,382 --> 00:04:44,660
Daily, weekly or monthly.

38
00:04:46,010 --> 00:04:55,408
It is multi-tenant from the ground up. Organisations, sub-
organisations, and lookups that never cross an org boundary.

39
00:04:55,608 --> 00:05:02,534
Each hospital tunes its own model, its own retrieval, its own
sign-in policy.

40
00:05:02,734 --> 00:05:12,996
Partner systems integrate over OAuth2, and everything runs in
a private subnet with encryption at rest and TLS in front.

41
00:05:14,350 --> 00:05:23,172
ClinIQ AI is decision support. The treating clinician’s
judgment takes precedence at all times.

42
00:05:23,372 --> 00:05:29,650
Clinical AI does not have to be a black box shipped from
someone else’s data centre.

43
00:05:29,850 --> 00:05:33,464
It can be something your institution owns.

44
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:39,336
Thank you for watching this quick demo of ClinIQ AI.

45
00:05:39,536 --> 00:05:45,142
To book a personalised demo, go to cliniqai.health.
